-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Optional learnability finding — review-43359e508d5bcb7f (2026-10-24)
+
+Source was pinned at SHA-256
+`50d56d456a9327798fc4aece3381315a09559d7fc996ec1daba826be2378568c`.
+A reusable finite-rival probe now lives at `workspace/learnability_probe.py`,
+with a focused regression in `tests/test_learnability_probe.py`.
+
+Across 256 deterministic hard-band lessons with three demonstrations and the
+next sample as query, nine lessons left a declared query-changing rival alive:
+seven `center_in_slots`, one `shapes_area_ascending`, and one
+`shapes_area_descending`. Seed 31 is the retained representative: top-left and
+centered slot alignment produce identical outputs for samples 0, 1, and 2, but
+differ at 72 cells on sample 3. The independent mirror matches all four retained
+canonical labels, and protected Racket reproduced all four seed-31 outputs.
+
+No production repair was selected in this optional pass. A constructive repair
+should schedule at least one demonstration whose shapes have unequal bounding
+boxes with an odd padding difference (to separate top-left from centering), and
+at least one demonstration whose top-to-bottom order conflicts with area order.
+Re-run the retained probe against every cyclic teaching window before integration.
+Imported associated notes remain in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
